 - **Avoid Flagship Burn on L0 Tasks**: Standard coding assistants frequently waste expensive flagship reasoning tokens on basic single-line formatting, regex syntax checks, or documentation typo fixes. Routing Level 0 tasks to economy models reduces token spend significantly on daily ad-hoc queries.
 - **Avoid Reasoning Failures on Hard Tasks**: Conversely, under-powering database migrations (Expand-Contract) or authentication boundary redesigns with lightweight models causes expensive defect repair loops. Deploying deep reasoning models exclusively on Level 2/3 work provides a verification standard for intended zero-downtime safety while keeping total aggregate token budgets lean.
 
+### Ceremony Artifact Overhead (not yet measured)
+
+The static and per-task figures above cover instruction-file payloads only; they do not cover the artifacts a task writes as it runs. **Per-level ceremony artifact overhead is not yet measured, so no figure is published for it here.**
+
+The artifacts in scope are the execution task record ([`templates/execution-task-record-template.md`](../templates/execution-task-record-template.md)), the execution checkpoint ([`templates/execution-checkpoint-template.md`](../templates/execution-checkpoint-template.md)), and the execution handoff ([`templates/execution-handoff-template.md`](../templates/execution-handoff-template.md)). Measurement is tracked in [issue #607](https://github.com/lowqualityloey/promptkit-os/issues/607). Until that lands, treat ceremony artifact cost as unquantified rather than free, and do not read the tables above as covering it.
